# Round draftgate: the chosen draft width (BLOOMERY_MTP_WIDTH=cost, the new default) against the fixed
# width, Qwen3.8 MTP decode on this tree's build. Same binary, lever arms.
# Band [derived, the draftgate report's last section]: on this box the gate keeps k = 3 on prose and
# en chat (r2/r3 within the margin), so cost runs the fixed width plus the selector's warm-up and a
# store walk per closed plain pass (about 3 % of a step on the few closed passes): prose P512
# -0.5..+0.5 %, en chat +0.1..+0.9 %. The gain is on a weak-host machine (W 2.7-3.0), which this box
# does not reach. As an ab card that band holds 0, so it is read as not slower by more than the margin.
kind: noninf
question: does the chosen draft width cost Qwen3.8 MTP decode against the fixed width on this box?
term: decode tok/s @ depth 512 and 4096, BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp, A6000, place a -
  (cost - fixed) / fixed, paired by round
unit: %
predict: -0.5..+0.9
rounds: 14
sd: 0.6 % same-binary per round, AGENTS.md 「Know the ruler」
condition: just depth-gpu-qwen4exp in one lease on this tree's build, order rotated every round,
  arms 512@BLOOMERY_MTP_WIDTH=cost 512@BLOOMERY_MTP_WIDTH=fixed 4096@BLOOMERY_MTP_WIDTH=cost
  4096@BLOOMERY_MTP_WIDTH=fixed; BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV holds BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp; each cost arm prints
  its `mtp width` record (windows, widths, e); no [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] row
decide-in: keep cost as the default width
decide-below: set the default to fixed for 0.2.6 and open the chain-cut round (stop the chain at k)
  before cost becomes the default again
decide-above: read the width records - a gate that closed on this box means the selector found a
  cheaper width than the derivation holds; re-derive W for this box
